WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.137
Step ten makes it repeatable.

2
00:00:02.137 --> 00:00:05.643
The kit compares each
run with the last: new,

3
00:00:05.643 --> 00:00:09.950
regressed, fixed, still open,
and no longer evaluated.

4
00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:11.938
That last class matters most.

5
00:00:11.938 --> 00:00:16.901
A finding the tool skipped this time
isn't fixed: fix the run and run it again.

6
00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:19.594
Runs from different tool
versions are refused

7
00:00:19.594 --> 00:00:22.150
until someone records
a review of the change.

8
00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:27.090
Then seal the evidence: each output
folder becomes a chained record with its

9
00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:30.775
controls, every file's hash,
and the previous record's hash,

10
00:00:30.775 --> 00:00:33.363
which the I S S O can
check without the kit.

11
00:00:33.363 --> 00:00:38.936
The cadence is design guidance from the
day-two runbook in Compliance Automation and

12
00:00:38.936 --> 00:00:42.470
Day-2 Operations: monthly,
after each remediation wave,

13
00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:44.825
before a tool upgrade, and quarterly.

14
00:00:44.825 --> 00:00:49.827
Learn's weekly digest playbook comes with
two cautions: report counts, not its

15
00:00:49.827 --> 00:00:55.130
pass rate, and whether it runs against three
point one point oh isn't yet specified.
